# SPA fallback for Cloudflare Pages and Netlify, which both read this file.
#
# Routing is client-side (BrowserRouter), so only / and the asset paths exist on
# the host. Without this rule a shared /result/<id> link, or the installed PWA
# fetching its start_url /scan on a cold cache, gets the host's 404 page
# instead of the app.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the browser must keep the path it asked for, because
# that path is what the router reads.
/*  /index.html  200
